#1 Terminal #2 \app(#1, #2, 400, 300, "foot", launch: "foot")
A terminal figure: the caption between #1 and #2 is ordinary prose, and
the statement reserves a 400x300 slot in the page flow.

Prose between figures exercises the text layout. Pages renumber every
marker key below this point when the line above it is edited.

#3 Editor #4 \app(#3, #4, 410, 310, "kgx*")
A second figure, bound by an app-id glob: "kgx*" claims kgx and any
app id starting with kgx.

#5 Chat #6 \app(#5, #6, 350, 250, "chat")
A third figure. Sizes are logical px (== pt at zoom 1); keep them
inside the text column or tier-1 diagnostics flag an overflow.
